{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And a peace-offering</b> — singular, for they offer up to HaShem. The plural form is <b>shallamim</b>; the singular form is <b>shalam</b> [construct]." "<b>And the fatlings (umeri'akhem)</b> — according to our master Rabbenu Hayyim, of blessed memory: from the language of the Mishnah, 'its fat is forbidden.' And it is not a species unto itself, as the Gaon [Saadia], of blessed memory, said: that its fat is permitted, and he explained it in the Arabic tongue as <i>jamus</i>. And it is not found in these lands, and it is larger than the ox and resembles it."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved the Hebrew grammatical argument as best the terse text allows; the point concerns singular vs. plural forms of the word for 'peace-offering,' but the compressed syntax makes the exact reasoning difficult to render fluently."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:13.841267601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}